### Relation to Rule JIRA.0

Rule JIRA.0 (`jira_bug_agent.mdc`) governs the **Experiments board** workflow only. Rule PHOENIX-BUG.0 covers Phoenix Phase 2 **Internal Bug** tickets and **External** standalone Bugs on any visible project except the denylist in this file. The two rules do not conflict — Experiments stays on `jira-bug`.

---

### Ticket creation — mandatory sequence (order is critical)

After user Agree, the agent MUST execute all steps in this exact order:

1. **Step 5a** — `createJiraIssue` (obtain issue key).

   - **Split ADF (Internal, External with 10103):** **full Tier 1 colored Key details ADF** in **`customfield_10103`** (Description first, Option A TL;DR, Option B Actual bullets, API `codeBlock` evidence, screenshot embed when **5b** succeeds — any Backend/Frontend/DB label); standard **`description`** omitted or empty; **one** minimal stub retry if create requires Description. **MUST NOT** put full bug body in standard `description`.

   - **Legacy Ph2 (no `customfield_10103`):** full markdown **`description`** only.

2. **Step 5b** — upload screenshot **before the embed**: run `attach-screenshot-to-jira.ps1` via Shell; capture `ATTACHMENT_FILENAME`, `ATTACHMENT_ID`, **`ATTACHMENT_MEDIA_UUID`**, `ATTACHMENT_WIDTH`, `ATTACHMENT_HEIGHT`; the script auto-converts WebP/BMP/TIFF to PNG. `ATTACHMENT_MEDIA_UUID` is the **only** valid value for ADF `media.attrs.id` — the numeric attachment id is rejected and Jira silently drops the node

3. **Step 5c** — **Split ADF:** **mandatory once when 5b uploaded an image** (exit 0), run **before 5d**; otherwise **conditional** on **5d** failure. `editJiraIssue` with **`customfield_10103` only** (no `description` in payload); max two attempts; MCP only — no Shell REST issue update. Content is the **same** Tier 1 ADF as 5a plus the `mediaSingle` — no other text, colour, order, or mark may change. **Legacy Ph2:** **mandatory** colored ADF on **`description`** after **5b**.

4. **Step 5d (split ADF boards)** — `getJiraIssue` with `expand=renderedFields`; verify **`customfield_10103`** Tier 1 structure (Description + TL;DR, Actual bullets, API codeBlocks, colors, content) and **report** the screenshot outcome. When an image was uploaded, a real image embed is required — a filename text line is a **fail**, reported as *attached only — not embedded*. When no image was provided, the screenshot criterion does not apply.

**Why Step 5b before the embed:** Step 5a cannot reference an attachment that does not exist yet; the media UUID only becomes available after upload.

**Screenshots are optional.** No image → no 5c on screenshot grounds, no screenshot criterion at 5d, no warning, and bug creation is never blocked.

**Rationale:** Split ADF authoritative body is **Description formatted** (`customfield_10103`). **`customfield_10103` MUST follow Tier 1 Key details template** — Description first, Option A TL;DR, Option B Actual bullets, API `codeBlock` evidence, screenshot embed when **5b** succeeds (any Backend/Frontend/DB label; not UI-only). Colored marks on standard **`description`** corrupt that panel. **5c** is the only step that can place the image in Key details, so it is mandatory whenever an image exists.

**Verified media node (PHN-4249, attachment 70014):** `mediaSingle` with `layout: "center"`, `width: 647`, `widthType: "pixel"`; inner `media` with `type: "file"`, `id: <ATTACHMENT_MEDIA_UUID>`, `collection: ""`, plus intrinsic `width` / `height`.

**Screenshot format:** `attach-screenshot-to-jira.ps1` automatically converts non-PNG/JPG formats (WebP, BMP, TIFF, etc.) to PNG using `System.Drawing`. If conversion fails, the original file is uploaded as-is.

